It builds on these upstream projects; their packages and model files are downloaded rather than vendored:

- TensorFold (https://github.com/ashhart/TensorFold), Apache License 2.0, Copyright 2026 TensorFold
  contributors. The image installs it at the commit pinned in scripts/config.sh; patches/ are changes to that
  commit and are offered under the same license.
- llama.cpp (https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp), MIT License, Copyright (c) 2023-2026 The ggml authors.
  The baseline image builds it at the commit pinned in scripts/config.sh.
- d1-3B and its GGUF files (https://huggingface.co/LiquidAI/d1-3B), LFM Open License v1.0, Liquid AI, Inc.
  The weights are downloaded from Hugging Face by the scripts and are never part of this repository. The
  decision prompt format the engine builds follows the model's own prompt.py.
- The int4 range search follows the idea of llama.cpp's k-quants (make_qkx2_quants), reimplemented.
- The bench picture is COCO val2017 image 39769 (https://cocodataset.org), fetched at bench time and not
  redistributed; it keeps its owner's license.
- Fast Decisions (https://huggingface.co/datasets/fastino/fast-decisions), Apache License 2.0, Fastino. Its files
  are downloaded at the revision pinned in checksums/fast-decisions.sha256. results/calibration/answers.jsonl
  repeats the dataset's row ids, task and label names and gold labels, but none of its texts.
